---
const lanes = [
  {
    id: "auto",
    name: "Auto-merge",
    who: "Evidence checks alone",
    examples: ["Internal refactor with no contract change", "New tests that add coverage", "Docs"],
  },
  {
    id: "judge",
    name: "Judge",
    who: "The verifying judge",
    examples: ["Additive contract change", "New internal dependency", "Moderate blast radius"],
  },
  {
    id: "person",
    name: "Human",
    who: "A person, reading the semantic report",
    examples: ["Auth, payments or personal data", "A new outside vendor", "Breaking contract changes"],
  },
  {
    id: "blocked",
    name: "Blocked",
    who: "Nobody, until it's fixed",
    examples: ["Writes outside scope", "Secrets in code", "Tests weakened without approval"],
  },
];
---

<section class="section wrap lanes" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="lanes-title">Every change gets a lane.</h2>
  <p class="prose lead">
    Every change and every request for more access gets a risk score, and the score decides who looks
    at it. The classifier weighs what changed, where it lives, how many components depend on it, how
    well the evidence covers it, the history of that area, and anything new, like a new outside service
    or a new kind of data leaving the system.
  </p>

  <div class="board" role="list">
    {
      lanes.map((l) => (
        <div class={`lane lane-${l.id}`} role="listitem">
          <div class="lane-head">
            <h3 class="lane-name">
              {l.id === "blocked" && <span class="no-entry" aria-hidden="true" />}
              {l.name}
            </h3>
            <p class="lane-who">{l.who}</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="lane-strips" role="list">
            {l.examples.map((e) => (
              <li class={`strip lane-strip ${l.id === "person" ? "is-person" : ""}`}>{e}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="rules">
    <div>
      <p class="subhead">Rules are a floor</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Start with explicit rules, add a learned model once there is outcome data. A model can move a change
        up a lane, never below the lane a rule assigns. “Anything touching auth goes to a person” can't be
        overridden by a model that thinks the change looks fine.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="subhead">The rules of the game always go to a person</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Changes to test assertions, CI pipelines, permission policies, risk labels, the judge's configuration
        and declared contracts. Agents can propose them; only people approve them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="subhead">Measure the misses</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Sample auto-merged changes for human audit. A slow review is a cost, but a missed risk is an incident,
        so false negatives get far more attention than false positives.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .board {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 15rem), 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 7%, var(--board));
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    padding: 0.75rem;
  }

  .lane {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lane-head {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--lane-color);
  }

  .lane-auto {
    --lane-color: var(--go);
  }

  .lane-judge {
    --lane-color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .lane-person {
    --lane-color: var(--buff-band);
  }

  .lane-blocked {
    --lane-color: var(--stop);
  }

  .lane-name {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-stretch: 115%;
    font-weight: 760;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .lane-who {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .lane-strips {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .lane-strip {
    --band: var(--lane-color);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .no-entry {
    width: 1rem;
    height: 1rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--stop);
    position: relative;
    flex: none;
  }

  .no-entry::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 22%;
    right: 22%;
    top: calc(50% - 1.5px);
    height: 3px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border-radius: 1px;
  }

  .rules {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 3vw, 4rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.75rem clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 2vw, 3rem);
  }

  .rules .muted {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
